    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW24JtvEoxLqeT8owZh2UKGVr)_\n\nFollow-up to #329 and #342: two new columns for the booksection/incollection tables.\n\n## What changes\n- `:bibtex` column (\"BibTeX\"):\n  - lists the citation keys of `ROAM_REFS` as `sp-bib:` links; RET or a click opens the entry in the `.bib` file (`citar-open-entry`);\n  - `embark-act` on a key offers the citar actions (entry, files, notes, links, copy reference) through a new embark target finder returning a `citar-key` target; it requires `citar-embark` when embark loads (`sp-citations` already installs it with `:ensure`).\n- `:dt-page` column (\"DT page\"):\n  - takes the `crossref` root of each key, its file (`citar-get-files`), and that file's DEVONthink record (same single JXA lookup as `:devonthink`, only when DEVONthink is running);\n  - links to `x-devonthink-item://UUID?page=N`, text \"p. 41\"; `N` is the first number of `pub-pages` plus an offset, counted from 0 (same convention as `sp-reading` in #343);\n  - offset: option `sp-collec-query-dt-page-offset` (default 0), overridden by a `pdf-offset` meta key on the book/collection note;\n  - a roman-numeral `pub-pages` links to the PDF (\"open\").\n- Both are now default columns of the book table (`sp-collec-query-book-columns`).\n- Literate doc updated in bullets; no CHANGELOG edits.\n\n## Tested\n- Emacs 29.3 batch, citar and Vulpea stubbed: 5 new ERT tests (27/27 in `sp-collection-query-tables-test.el`, book tests 7/7).\n\n## Not tested (please try on the Mac)\n- Nothing against DEVONthink: `?page=N` being 0-based and opening the right page is taken from the DEVONthink item-link convention used in #343, not verified here.\n- The printed-page to PDF-page offset is a guess (0) until you set `pdf-offset` on a book.\n- `embark-act` with real `citar-embark`, and the exc/vui renderers, were not run.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9zQ9SjpxWCzkgTYYM)_",
